                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I see the positive reviews for this game and wonder what I'm missing... I am actually the person this game is really aiming for. Love puzzle games, enjoy platformers, but I just find this game unbelievably tedious, and frequently frustrating. You are basically using awkward controls to try to slowly move your way through levels without running into anything that will kill you. It is difficult, but in the wrong way. It is basically difficult just because trying to creep through these levels can be so painful, the desire to go faster becomes overwhelming, which ends up getting you killed. You then restart the level or start back at the last check point and try to do the same tedious section again, but slower so you don't die.\n\nI can understand that there may be people out there patient enough to get a little enjoyment out of this but I just can't imagine there are that many. I have not really had the urge to smash a controller / mouse in years and this game had me there in under 2 hours. \n\nIf you would like some more info, feel free to check out my video below for my full impressions (although if I am being honest, it's mostly me just trying to explain how tedious the whole thing is).\n\n\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=757766193\n",
